<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia March 1-20 palm oil exports 391,599t-SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia March 1-20 palm oil exports 391,599t-SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for March 1-20 were 391,599 against 269,684 in February 1-20.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 120,412 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 153,230 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 28,325 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products were 49,632 tonnes.  </p>
<p>China was the main buyer during the period, taking 59,750 tonnes, followed by Pakistan 56,670 tonnes, U.S. at 27,985 tonnes and Egypt 23,500.</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 62,542 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-7510)</p>
